  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nMid level ridge axis is centered over the central conus this \nafternoon. Embedded perturbations along the northern periphery have \nresulted in clusters of storms towards northern Nebraska. At the \nsfc, temps are quickly heating into the upper 90s and should peak \nnear 100 this afternoon as southerly winds sustain near 10 mph. \nGiven the weaker mixing, dewpoints hover around 70 degrees, \nresulting in peak heat indices around 105 today. No changes were \nmade to the Extreme Heat Warning as the ridge will persist in the \nregion through at least Tuesday evening. \n\nFocus turns to Sunday afternoon as latest short term CAM guidance is \nfalling closer in line with the latest NAM/GFS/EC on a cluster of \nstorms forming in the Dakotas before dropping south and west along a \nfrontal boundary into northern MO. Majority of convection appears \nconfined to MO, but could still see a few storms develop across far \neastern KS through early evening.  BLCAPE is decent by this time \nnear 2000 J/KG while effective shear weakens further west and south \ninto our area so I would not expect storms to maintain severe \nintensity for a prolonged period. If storms develop, main hazard \nwith these storms would be gusty winds up to 60 mph.\n\nCannot rule out a similar setup on Monday with the isolated storm \npotential, however given mid level heights increasing north and \nnortheast during the day, I opted to keep pops below 10 percent for \nnow. Pattern shift commences Tuesday as an upper low tracks across \nCanada, shifting the ridge eastward while developing low level \nsouthwest troughing in the western high plains. A cold front enters \nnorthern Kansas by late Tuesday evening, developing a line of \nscattered storms towards Nebraska and portions of north central \nareas overnight. Additional northern stream troughing will determine \nhow far south the front progresses Wednesday into Thursday as \nensemble clusters are varying on the speed of the front and \nsubsequent precip chances/temperatures. However given the synoptic \nsetup and boundary settled somewhere in the area, low chances for \noccasional showers and storms remains reasonable Wednesday through \nFriday. Most locations will likely remain dry. Cooler temps \ngradually make into the forecast area by late week, returning highs \nto near 90 degrees Thursday onward.",
